/-!
# Gorenstein local rings on the blowup of a rational double point

Let `(R, 𝔪)` be a Noetherian local ring of Krull dimension `d` whose maximal ideal is generated
by `d + 1` elements and which contains a field mapping onto its residue field, and suppose the
completion `R^` is a domain. Then `R` is Gorenstein.

This is the Gorenstein propagation step of Section 54.12 of the source, in the shape the blowup
of a rational double point delivers it. The source obtains the Gorenstein property of the
singularities of the blowup from a description of the dualizing sheaf of the blowup; the route
here is the shorter one of `RationalDoublePoints/CompletedHypersurface.lean`, which only uses the
shape of the completed local ring. Three hypotheses are all that is needed at the blowup, and
each of them is available there: the completion is a domain by clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0BG7],
the dimension is two, and the embedding dimension is three.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.isGorensteinLocalRing_of_isDomain_adicCompletion`: the propagation step as a
  statement about a single Noetherian local ring. All hypotheses are stated for `R` itself; they
  are transported to `R^` inside the proof.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RationalDoublePointSituation.isGorensteinLocalRing_stalk_blowUp`: the local
  ring at a closed point of the blowup of `Spec(A)` in the maximal ideal, for `A` the ring of a
  Situation [Stacks, Tag 0BGC], is Gorenstein.

## Implementation notes

Why the hypotheses are stated at `R` and not at `R^`. Writing them at `R^` would make
`IsLocalRing R^` — and therefore `IsNoetherianRing R` — part of the elaboration of the statement
itself, which for the local ring of a blowup is not an instance. Stated at `R` they transport:
the maximal ideal of `R^` is generated by the image of `𝔪` ([Stacks, Tag 05GH]), so the images of
`d + 1` generators generate it, and the residue field of `R^` is the residue field of `R`, so a
field mapping onto the latter maps onto the former.

The descent of the Gorenstein property from `R^` to `R` is clause (1) of
`Stacks.Duality.isGorensteinLocalRing_iff_of_flat`, [Stacks, Tag 0BJL], for the completion map —
flat and local, with Noetherian source and target. It is used inline rather than through a named
lemma; the project's two existing copies of that one-line descent,
`Stacks.Curves.isGorensteinLocalRing_of_adicCompletion` and
`Stacks.Curves.isGorensteinLocalRing_adicCompletion`, are both private.

What is still a hypothesis. For the situation of Tag 0BGC the embedding dimension of the local
ring at a singular point of the blowup is the case `n = 1` of the source's dimension formula
`dim_κ(𝔪ⁿ/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹) = 2n + 1`, which the project does not prove; its Krull dimension is likewise not
computed here; and normality of the blowup of `Spec(A^)` in the maximal ideal of `A^`, which
clause (2) of Tag 0BG7 consumes, needs `A^` to define a rational singularity — clause (1) of
Tag 0BG7, which is absent. All three are carried in binders, so nothing here carries a
`@[stacks]` attribute: with those hypotheses added to the source's setup these statements say
less than the source does.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BGE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BGE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BGC](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BGC)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BG7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BG7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BJL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BJL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4Z)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory IsLocalRing

universe u v

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **Gorenstein propagation.** Let `(R, 𝔪)` be a Noetherian local ring of Krull dimension `d`
whose completion is a domain, whose maximal ideal is generated by `d + 1` elements, and which
receives a homomorphism from a field surjective onto its residue field. Then `R` is Gorenstein.

The completion `R^` is a complete local Noetherian domain of the same dimension, the images of
the generators generate its maximal ideal, and the field maps onto its residue field too, so
`AlgebraicGeometry.isGorensteinLocalRing_of_span_eq_maximalIdeal_of_ringKrullDim` presents it as
`κ[[x₁, …, x_{d+1}]]/(g)` and makes it Gorenstein. The property descends to `R` along the
completion map by [Stacks, Tag 0BJL].

For `d = 2` and three generators this is the Gorenstein propagation of Section 54.12: see
`AlgebraicGeometry.RationalDoublePointSituation.isGorensteinLocalRing_stalk_blowUp`. -/
public theorem isGorensteinLocalRing_of_isDomain_adicCompletion {R : Type u} [CommRing R]
    [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] {d : ℕ}
    (hdom : IsDomain (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R)) (K : Type v) [Field K] (f : K →+* R)
    (x : Fin (d + 1) → R)
    (hf : Function.Surjective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (maximalIdeal R)).comp f))
    (hx : Ideal.span (Set.range x) = maximalIdeal R)
    (hdim : ringKrullDim R = (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    Dualizing.IsGorensteinLocalRing R := by
  let : IsNoetherianRing (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) :=
    AdicCompletion.isNoetherianRing (maximalIdeal R)
  let : IsDomain (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) := hdom
  let : Module.Flat R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) :=
    AdicCompletion.flat_of_isNoetherian (maximalIdeal R)
  have hmax : maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) =
      Ideal.map (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R)) (maximalIdeal R) :=
    AdicCompletion.maximalIdeal_eq_map
  -- the images of the generators generate the maximal ideal of the completion
  have hx' : Ideal.span
      (Set.range fun i => algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) (x i)) =
      maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) := by
    rw [hmax, ← hx, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
    rfl
  -- the field maps onto the residue field of the completion
  have hf' : Function.Surjective
      ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R))).comp
        ((algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R)).comp f)) := by
    have hbij := AdicCompletion.residueField_map_bijective_of_fg
      (R := R) (maximalIdeal R).fg_of_isNoetherianRing
    intro z
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hbij.2 z
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hf w
    refine ⟨c, ?_⟩
    have hnat : ResidueField.map (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R))
        (residue R (f c)) =
        residue (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R)
          (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) (f c)) := rfl
    rw [show ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (maximalIdeal (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R))).comp
      ((algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R)).comp f)) c =
      residue (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R)
        (algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) (f c)) from rfl, ← hnat,
      show residue R (f c) = w from hc, hw]
  have hdim' : ringKrullDim (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) :=
    (_root_.ringKrullDim_adicCompletion_maximalIdeal (A := R)).symm.trans hdim
  have hcompl : Dualizing.IsGorensteinLocalRing (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) :=
    isGorensteinLocalRing_of_span_eq_maximalIdeal_of_ringKrullDim K
      ((algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R)).comp f)
      (fun i => algebraMap R (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R) (x i)) hf' hx' hdim'
  exact ((Dualizing.isGorensteinLocalRing_iff_of_flat R
    (AdicCompletion (maximalIdeal R) R)).mp hcompl).1

namespace RationalDoublePointSituation

/-- **The local rings at the closed points of the blowup of a rational double point are
Gorenstein.** Let `A` be the ring of a Situation [Stacks, Tag 0BGC] whose completion defines a
rational singularity, and let `x` be a closed point of the blowup of `Spec(A)` in the maximal
ideal at which the local ring has Krull dimension two, embedding dimension three, and contains a
field mapping onto its residue field. Then that local ring is Gorenstein.

Clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0BG7] makes the completion of the local ring at `x` a normal domain,
and `AlgebraicGeometry.isGorensteinLocalRing_of_isDomain_adicCompletion` concludes. The
hypothesis on the completion of `A` is clause (1) of Tag 0BG7, which the project does not prove;
it is what feeds [Stacks, Tag 0B4Z] at `A^`, the other three inputs of which — `A^` a normal
domain, Nagata, of dimension two — are supplied by the situation, by completeness, and by the
invariance of Krull dimension under completion.

See the module docstring for why there is no `@[stacks]` attribute. -/
public theorem isGorensteinLocalRing_stalk_blowUp (S : RationalDoublePointSituation.{u})
    (hrat :
      letI : IsNormalDomain (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A) S.A) :=
        S.completion_normalDomain
      DefinesRationalSingularity (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A) S.A))
    (x : blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A))
    (hx : IsClosed ({x} : Set (blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A))))
    (hdim : ringKrullDim ((blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A)).presheaf.stalk x) = 2)
    (K : Type v) [Field K] (f : K →+* (blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A)).presheaf.stalk x)
    (y : Fin 3 → (blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A)).presheaf.stalk x)
    (hf : Function.Surjective ((Ideal.Quotient.mk
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A)).presheaf.stalk x))).comp f))
    (hy : Ideal.span (Set.range y) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A)).presheaf.stalk x)) :
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (Spec (.of S.A)) := isLocallyNoetherian_Spec.mpr inferInstance
    letI : IsLocallyNoetherian (blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A)) :=
      LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (blowUpToBase (maximalIdealSheaf S.A))
    Dualizing.IsGorensteinLocalRing
      ((blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A)).presheaf.stalk x) := by
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian (Spec (.of S.A)) := isLocallyNoetherian_Spec.mpr inferInstance
  let : IsLocallyNoetherian (blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf S.A)) :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (blowUpToBase (maximalIdealSheaf S.A))
  let : IsNoetherianRing (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A) S.A) :=
    AdicCompletion.isNoetherianRing (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A)
  let : IsNormalDomain (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A) S.A) :=
    S.completion_normalDomain
  -- Tag 0B4Z at the completion: the blowup of `Spec(A^)` in the maximal ideal is normal
  have hnormal : IsNormal
      (blowUp (maximalIdealSheaf (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A) S.A))) :=
    isNormal_blowUp_maximalIdeal_of_forall_isIntegrallyClosed_pow
      (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A) S.A) fun n =>
        isIntegrallyClosed_maximalIdeal_pow_of_definesRationalSingularity
          (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal S.A) S.A)
          IsNagataRing.of_isPrecomplete_maximalIdeal
          ((_root_.ringKrullDim_adicCompletion_maximalIdeal (A := S.A)).symm.trans S.dimension_two)
          hrat n
  -- Tag 0BG7, clause (2): the completed local ring at `x` is a normal domain
  have hnd := isNormalDomain_adicCompletion_stalk_blowUp_maximalIdeal S.A hnormal x hx
  exact isGorensteinLocalRing_of_isDomain_adicCompletion (d := 2) hnd.isDomain K f y hf hy
    (by rw [hdim]; rfl)

end RationalDoublePointSituation

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
